  "pro_time_note": "Price `answer` with splits/time_costs.json. Upper bound from the human run: 66.683 s from start to first portal enter, which also includes whatever else the runner collected (beds) before entering.",
  "why": "Both ruined-portal chests sit next to the portal: chest_portal_b has 11 obsidian and 6 iron ingots, chest_portal_a has 4 obsidian and 1 flint. That is 15 obsidian, plus 1 iron ingot + 1 flint for flint and steel (crafted in the 2x2 inventory grid, no table needed). The ruined frame already holds 3 usable obsidian for a 4x5 frame shifted one block along Z, so completing it takes 7 placements and avoids the crying obsidian. The village chest (6 obsidian, iron pickaxe) is not needed just to enter the Nether. No obsidian has to be mined, and there is no diamond pickaxe to mine it with.",
  "trap": "Mining obsidian (impossible here: no diamond pickaxe), looking for lava, or looting every village chest for food and armor before going to the portal.",
